Package: shadowfetch-firewatchd
Version: 2.1.2-1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Shadowfetch Project <signing@shadowfetch.com>
Installed-Size: 83
Depends: python3, python3-dbus, python3-gi, python3-psutil, dbus, smartmontools, nvme-cli
Recommends: python3-pynvml, lm-sensors
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://shadowfetch.com/linux/
Description: Shadowfetch Firewatch telemetry daemon
 The always-on sensor source behind the Firewatch page of the Shadowfetch
 Control Center and the single source of the ELI/flame level that Ember
 Mode consumes. Publishes org.shadowfetch.Firewatch1 on the system bus:
 CPU/RAM/PSI, hwmon temperatures and fans, RAPL package watts, whole-GPU
 stats, a per-application heat map with human display names and icons,
 local llama-server model usage with tokens per second, storage health
 via smartctl and nvme smart-log, and thermal-throttle events.
 .
 The daemon is read-only against the system and generates zero network
 traffic except polling llama-server metrics on 127.0.0.1. NVIDIA
 telemetry uses python3-pynvml when present (a Recommends, never a hard
 dependency) and reports whole-GPU statistics only.
